[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711380846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-3711380846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":3711380846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dNy1u","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T17:24:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T17:24:33Z","body":"@bruvzg Do you think we can add support for the feature in iOS as well?\r\n\r\nIf yes, can you take a look at the proposed APIs and see if they match the iOS set of APIs for PiP.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711380846/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711688325","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-3711688325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":3711688325,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dO96F","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T18:53:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T18:53:01Z","body":"I'm not super familiar with PiP API on iOS, but it should be possible to implement.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711688325/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711725275","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-3711725275","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":3711725275,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dPG7b","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T19:04:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T19:04:34Z","body":"> `pip_mode_enter`\r\n\r\nShould it take `window_id` as argument?\r\n\r\nCurrently, iOS implementation only support one window, but new versions of iPadOS have pretty much full support for multi window apps. And it's common behavior to detach only a specific element of the app as PIP (e.g, detach video player from the browser while still using the main interface).\r\n\r\n> This can be combined with pip_mode_set_aspect_ratio, we can have a single method pip_mode_configure(aspect_ratio: Vector2, auto_enter_on_background: bool).\r\n\r\nI do not think there's API to automatically activate it in background, but it should be doable from `applicationWillResignActive`. Neither there's `aspect_ratio`, but frame size can be set, so it should be possible to use the same API.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711725275/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711731824","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-3711731824","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":3711731824,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dPIhw","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T19:06:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T19:06:32Z","body":"There probably should be `bool is_pip_mode_available()` as well, since I think it's not possible to activate it (at least there's iOS API to check if it's available).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3711731824/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715812413","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-3715812413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":3715812413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7desw9","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T18:25:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T18:25:32Z","body":"> I do not think there's API to automatically activate it in background, but it should be doable from applicationWillResignActive. Neither there's aspect_ratio, but frame size can be set, so it should be possible to use the same API.\r\n\r\nI think it'd be better to keep the configuration APIs separate instead of merging them into a single `pip_mode_configure(...)` method. \r\nThe former approach allows us to add additional configuration options based on platform capabilities or user feedback, whereas the latter approach forces us to deprecate the existing `pip_mode_configure(...)` every time we want to add a new configuration option. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715812413/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715829281","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-3715829281","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":3715829281,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dew4h","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T18:30:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T18:30:09Z","body":"> There probably should be `bool is_pip_mode_available()` as well, since I think it's not possible to activate it (at least there's iOS API to check if it's available).\r\n\r\n@bruvzg In the current Android implementation, the `DisplayServer#has_feature(FEATURE_PIP_MODE)` check plays that role. \r\nIt checks whether:\r\n- The device supports PiP based on Android version and device capabilities\r\n- And if the current Android activity is configured for PiP support based on the Android manifest declaration\r\n\r\nThis allows developers to just make one check before using PiP:\r\n```\r\nif DisplayServer.has_feature(DisplayServer.FEATURE_PIP_MODE):\r\n    # Configure the aspect ratio, or omit this call to keep the default\r\n    DisplayServer.pip_mode_set_aspect_ratio(1, 1)\r\n    DisplayServer.pip_mode_enter()\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3715829281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3902356999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-3902356999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":3902356999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7omT4H","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-14T18:56:53Z","updated_at":"2026-02-14T18:56:53Z","body":"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/841aa720-c423-43b0-8427-98b2a0e27790\r\n\r\nTested this PR now, everything looks good and is working as expected.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3902356999/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4033910269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-4033910269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":4033910269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wcJX9","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T19:29:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T19:29:36Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4033910269/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189097764","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-4189097764","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":4189097764,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75sI8k","user":{"login":"Birdulon","id":5397662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTc2NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5397662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon","html_url":"https://github.com/Birdulon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Birdulon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T15:55:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-05T15:55:53Z","body":"Very cool! I saw the dev snapshot announcement and this caught my eye:\r\n\r\n> Note that picture-in-picture does not permit interacting with the application while it is in this mode, so this feature is most useful for applications and games that have sections that don’t require real-time input (idle games, autobattlers, etc.).\r\n\r\nA quick skim of the Android docs suggests that [at least 3](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#getMaxNumPictureInPictureActions()) custom controls (well, tappable icons) can be declared for PiP windows ( https://developer.android.com/design/ui/mobile/guides/home-screen/picture-in-picture#controls )\r\nI haven't played around with this yet, and the controls [seem very limited at a glance](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/RemoteAction), but even three simple buttons with unknown jitter/latency could be very useful compared to needing to exit PiP to do anything.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189097764/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189118898","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-4189118898","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":4189118898,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75sOGy","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T16:07:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-05T16:07:48Z","body":"> Very cool! I saw the dev snapshot announcement and this caught my eye:\r\n> \r\n> > Note that picture-in-picture does not permit interacting with the application while it is in this mode, so this feature is most useful for applications and games that have sections that don’t require real-time input (idle games, autobattlers, etc.).\r\n> \r\n> A quick skim of the Android docs suggests that [at least 3](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#getMaxNumPictureInPictureActions()) custom controls (well, tappable icons) can be declared for PiP windows ( https://developer.android.com/design/ui/mobile/guides/home-screen/picture-in-picture#controls ) I haven't played around with this yet, and the controls [seem very limited at a glance](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/RemoteAction), but even three simple buttons with unknown jitter/latency could be very useful compared to needing to exit PiP to do anything.\r\n\r\nYeah, I was thinking the same, this would complete the feature. @m4gr3d if you're on board with the idea, I'd like to take a look at it next week.\r\n\r\n@Birdulon it would be good if you could create a small proposal for this. If for some unknown reason we can't work on it for 4.7, it'll be useful for tracking.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189118898/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4189148536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114505#issuecomment-4189148536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114505","id":4189148536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75sVV4","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":